    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n62946" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λῆξις</span></b>  (B), <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εως</span>,
			ἡ, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λήγω</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>cessation</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μόχθων, ἀνέμων</span>, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Eu.</u>
				505
			</span></i> (lyr.), <i><span class="en">
				A.R.
				1.1086
			</span></i>; of the flow of a river, <i><span class="en">
				Ph.
				1.175
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῆς ἐνεργείας λῆξιν λαμβανούσης</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Gal.
					<u>Phil.Hist.</u>
					17
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				M.Ant.
				9.21
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>death, decase,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				PMasp.
				19.6
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(vi A.D.)</span>, etc. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> Gramm., <i>termination</i>, <i><span class="en">
				A.D.
				<u>Synt.</u>
				104.28
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λ. ἡ εἰς σ̄</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Adv.</u>
					195.27
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			<i>end, extremity</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοῦ κόλου</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Sor.
					1.7
				</span></i>
			.</div>
